# Caddy reverse proxy -> bustracker (waitress on 127.0.0.1:5000)
#
# Install to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile. Caddy fetches and renews the Let's Encrypt
# certificate automatically, so no port 443 config or certbot is needed.
#
# Namecheap DNS: A record  @  ->  <server public IP>
#                A record  www ->  <server public IP>
# Certificate issuance needs ports 80 + 443 reachable from the internet.
# Either open them in the OCI security list + the Ubuntu firewall, or skip
# Caddy entirely and use a Cloudflare Tunnel (no inbound ports at all).

popojiji.com {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5000
}

www.popojiji.com {
	redir https://popojiji.com{uri} permanent
}